cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "fem4m: A Finite Element Toolbox for MATLAB"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gedicke
    given-names: Joscha
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8448-0608"
    affiliation: "Institute for Numerical Simulation, University of Bonn"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23810422
repository-code: "https://github.com/fem4m/fem4m"
license: MIT
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-10-30
abstract: >-
        fem4m is a MATLAB toolbox for finite element methods in research and teaching. 
        Weak forms are written as strings that read like the integrals they stand for, 
        so a new discretization, error estimator or error norm is a single line. 
        Behind the strings sit the finite element classes (Lagrange, hp, Crouzeix-Raviart, 
        discontinuous Galerkin, Raviart-Thomas, Brezzi-Douglas-Marini, Nédélec, Argyris, 
        Hellan-Herrmann-Johnson, Arnold-Winther, ...), adaptive meshes in 2D, 3D and on surfaces, 
        multigrid and domain decomposition solvers, and several ready-made test problems, 
        most of them with exact solutions.
keywords:
  - finite element method
  - MATLAB